est.java:98` checks\",\"`ProductCatalogPageIntegrationTest.java:99` checks\"),\n(\"asserts, on line 89, that each target\",\"asserts, on line 90, that each target\"),\n(\"and, on line 94, that the target\",\"and, on line 96, that the target\"),\n(\"seeded description (line 74)\\n  and its image `src` (line 75).\",\"seeded description (line 75)\\n  and its image `src` (line 76).\"),\n(\"its name (line 73)\",\"its name (line 74)\"),\n(\"not just one (line 83)\",\"not just one (line 85)\"),\n(\"\\\"View Details\\\" (line 87), targeting\\n  `/products/<uuid>` (line 88)\",\"\\\"View Details\\\" (line 89), targeting\\n  `/products/<uuid>` (line 90)\"),\n(\"(lines 90-98)\",\"(lines 92-99)\"),\n(\"\\\"Product Catalog\\\" (line 107), the heading \\\"Our Products\\\" (line 108) and the breadcrumb\\n  \\\"Home / Products\\\" (line 109)\",\"\\\"Product Catalog\\\" (line 108), the heading \\\"Our Products\\\" (line 109) and the breadcrumb\\n  \\\"Home / Products\\\" (line 110)\"),\n]:\n    assert a in s, a; s=s.replace(a,b)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nsed -n 92,97p ../../src/test-integration/java/dev/domaincentric/sample/ecommerce/product/ProductCatalogPageIntegrationTest.java","description":"Fix line numbers in judge.md"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":19,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I reviewed CAT-01 and the verdict is **pass**. It's written to `tasks/CAT-01/judge.md`.\n\nCAT-01 is an adopted story, meaning the shop already had the behaviour. So the review checked one thing: whether each mapped test actually proves its scenario. I read every test against its Given/When/Then and found no defects.\n\n- **catalogue-lists-the-seeded-range:** the existing browser test `SeededCatalogE2ETest` opens the catalogue and checks for 21 cards.\n- **The other four scenarios:** each has an integration test in `ProductCatalogPageIntegrationTest`, which renders the catalogue page in the full application:\n  - **catalogue-is-in-name-order:** the titles are in character order and the first is `\"Bounded Context\" Enamel Pin`.\n  - **card-shows-name-description-and-image:** the \"Domain-Driven Design\" card shows its name, full description and image.\n  - **card-leads-to-the-product:** every card has a \"View Details\" link, and following it opens that product's page.\n  - **catalogue-page-heading:** the page title, heading and breadcrumb all match the scenario.\n- **Deliberate breaks:** each of the four small code changes used to make a test fail touches exactly what that test checks.\n\nThings the report records but that don't block:\n- **Missing seed file:** the story's Given names `seed-catalogue.json`, which doesn't exist in this repository; the 21 products are created in code. The plan had already flagged this. The behaviour is proved either way. If the story means this sample must load that file, the story needs correcting, not the code.\n- **Changes from elsewhere:** the diff also contains CAT-02's tests and the change that makes the browser tests start the shop themselves (from decision CAT-01-01). I didn't review those as part of this story.\n- **Reviews not run:** the architecture reviews (DDD, hexagonal, clean code, and the extra `dca-review`) were available, but I didn't run them because no production code changed. I didn't consult `dca-knowledge` either, since no finding depended on it.\n\nI changed no code and ran no other stages.","ttft_ms":3459,"type":"result","duration_ms":96828,"uuid":"35ba56da-e0de-47b1-ab6f-d3e0316a29a2","ttft_stream_ms":2235,"time_to_request_ms":197,"first_content_frame_ms":2235,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
